{"chunk_id": "73dc7137df5f", "text": "Krishna arrives at the Kuru court in great splendour, greeted with universal respect. Dhritarashtra, Bhishma, Drona, and the assembled kings rise in honour, and Krishna takes a golden seat after acknowledging each elder. Sages led by Narada appear in the sky, and Krishna insists they be formally welcomed before anyone else proceeds, reinforcing the court\u2019s duty to righteousness. Once silence falls, Krishna addresses Dhritarashtra with a powerful appeal for peace between the Kauravas and Pandavas. He praises the noble traditions of the Kuru lineage but warns that Duryodhana\u2019s greed and injustice threaten universal destruction. Krishna argues that Dhritarashtra still has the authority to restrain his sons and avert war. If the Kurus and Pandavas unite rather than fight, he says, their combined strength would make the kingdom invincible and bring prosperity to the entire realm.\nKrishna arrives at the Kuru court with great honor and urges Dhritarashtra to restrain Duryodhana and make peace with the Pandavas.\nThemes: diplomacy, royal court ceremony, peace vs war, moral counsel, family conflict", "vector": [0.014528787694871426, -0.014622694812715054, -0.006811626721173525, 0.004323085770010948, -0.005574063863605261, 0.021384013816714287, -0.006134153343737125, -0.02021688222885132, -0.016339855268597603, -0.010423700325191021, 0.018660705536603928, -0.007673561107367277, 0.002872554585337639, 0.01584348827600479, -0.014394634403288364, -0.00033580214949324727, 0.033135831356048584, -0.0196534376591444, 0.03294801712036133, -0.009437674656510353, -0.019009502604603767, -0.0003534097340889275, -0.003984348848462105, 0.00786137580871582, -0.016514254733920097, 0.03203577548265457, 0.013012857176363468, -0.017117943614721298, 0.014569033868610859, -0.022671883925795555, -0.012871995568275452, 0.01892901211977005, 0.011557294987142086, -0.011865846812725067, -0.014917831867933273, 0.007492454256862402, -0.003538289573043585, 